From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: defer freeform parent mapping until task geometry

A task relayout can temporarily remove all its layers, recreating its native
window. Mapping its background at the shared display size first generates a
compositor configure after the task frame arrives. configure_task mistakes
that bootstrap size for a user resize and expands the task to the display.
Reproduced with Google Play Store: 900x700 -> window recreation -> 2560x1400.

Leave decorated freeform parents unmapped until set_content_frame chooses
their task size. Other window modes retain their existing bootstrap path.
Original work for waydroid-nvidia; modifies Apache-2.0 hwcomposer sources.

diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
index 0859e77..dcc1596 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
@@ -896,6 +896,8 @@ void window::set_content_frame(hwc_rect_t frame) {
     if (!host_width || !host_height) {
         host_width = std::max(1, (int)ceil((frame.right - frame.left) / display->scale));
         host_height = std::max(1, (int)ceil((frame.bottom - frame.top) / display->scale));
+        if (dedicated_background_surface && bg_buffer)
+            wl_surface_attach(surface, bg_buffer, 0, 0);
     }
     if (xdg_surface)
         xdg_surface_set_window_geometry(xdg_surface, 0, 0, host_width, host_height);
@@ -1345,7 +1347,13 @@ window::create(struct display *display, bool use_subsurfaces, std::string appID,
     window->bg_buffer = wl_shm_pool_create_buffer(pool, 0, 1, 1, 4, WL_SHM_FORMAT_ARGB8888);
     wl_shm_pool_destroy(pool);
 
-    wl_surface_attach(window->surface, window->bg_buffer, 0, 0);
+    /* A freeform parent must not map at the shared display size. The first
+     * task frame attaches its background after choosing the task geometry.
+     * Otherwise relayout/recreation feeds the display-sized configure back
+     * through resize_task and enlarges the Android task again. */
+    if (!window->uses_task_geometry()) {
+        wl_surface_attach(window->surface, window->bg_buffer, 0, 0);
+    }
     wl_surface_damage(window->surface, 0, 0, INT32_MAX, INT32_MAX);
     wp_viewport_set_source(window->viewport, wl_fixed_from_int(0), wl_fixed_from_int(0), wl_fixed_from_int(1), wl_fixed_from_int(1));
     wp_viewport_set_destination(window->viewport, display->width, display->height);
